      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1100",
      "html": "<p>Tatia neivai (Ihering, 1930), family Auchenipteridae. Common name: Naive Tatia (Germany). Type locality: Rio Piracicaba, Piracicaba, São Paulo State, Brazil. Synonym: Glanidium neivai. Etymology: Tatia was named after the ichthyologist C. Tate Regan. Size: 57 mm (2.2\") SL. IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2018).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1100",
      "html": "<p>South America: Piracicaba River, São Paulo, Brazil. Also found in the La Plata basin: Paraná, Upper Paraná, Grande (Paraná), Uberaba, Tietê, Piracicaba (São Paulo), and Paraguay, Upper Paraguay, Cuiabá and Claro.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1100",
      "html": "<p>As the common name for this family, woodcat, implies, these fish like pieces of wood with crevices and gaps to squeeze into.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1100",
      "html": "<p>Mature males exhibit a modified anal fin copulatory organ.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1100",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
